1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,540
Built Different.

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:05,080
Case number zero zero nine.

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:08,120
The subject did not breathe for seventeen minutes.

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:09,565
April thirtieth,

5
00:00:09,265 --> 00:00:10,720
two thousand eight.

6
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,720
A live television stage.

7
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,360
A sphere of water.

8
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:15,960
A man inside it,

9
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:16,840
perfectly still.

10
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:18,460
And a judge from Guinness,

11
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,580
watching the clock.

12
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,640
Try it right now.

13
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:23,500
Hold your breath and count.

14
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,280
Then think about this.

15
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:27,920
He went seventeen minutes and four seconds.

16
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:30,180
How is that possible?

17
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,040
Exhibit one.

18
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:33,180
The failure.

19
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:34,820
Two years earlier,

20
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:35,520
in New York,

21
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,520
he lived for a week inside a sphere

22
00:00:37,220 --> 00:00:38,080
of water.

23
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:40,160
Then he tried to hold his breath while

24
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,160
working out of chains.

25
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,440
At seven minutes and eight seconds,

26
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:45,280
his body began to convulse.

27
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:47,180
Divers pulled him out.

28
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,880
Most people would call that the end of

29
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:50,420
the story.

30
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,900
He called it data.

31
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:53,760
Exhibit two.

32
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:54,900
The body.

33
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,640
By his own account,

34
00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:58,760
he dropped more than fifty pounds in about

35
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,500
three months.

36
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,280
A smaller body burns less oxygen.

37
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:04,840
He says his resting heart rate fell to

38
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,160
thirty-eight beats a minute.

39
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,380
He was not building muscle.

40
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:10,820
He was building a quieter machine.

41
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,740
Exhibit three.

42
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:13,920
The reflex.

43
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,700
Here is something you already carry.

44
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,880
Put your face in water and hold your

45
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:19,160
breath,

46
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:21,000
and your body changes the rules.

47
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,060
Your heart slows down.

48
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:25,380
The blood vessels in your arms and legs

49
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:25,860
tighten,

50
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,100
saving blood for the brain and the heart.

51
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:31,240
Your spleen squeezes out extra red blood cells.

52
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:33,220
Seals do this.

53
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,720
Whales do this.

54
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:35,980
You do this.

55
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:38,700
Most of us just never train it.

56
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,060
Exhibit four.

57
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,060
The burn.

58
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,320
Here is the strange part.

59
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,200
The desperate need to breathe is not your

60
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,660
body running out of oxygen.

61
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:50,580
It is carbon dioxide building up.

62
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,980
That burning in your chest is an alarm.

63
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,340
Not the fire.

64
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,360
He trained to sit inside that alarm and

65
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,280
stay calm.

66
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,000
Exhibit five.

67
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,480
The fine print.

68
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:03,160
Before he went under,

69
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:06,180
he breathed pure oxygen for about twenty-three minutes.

70
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,200
The rules allowed it.

71
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,320
It loaded his blood like a full tank

72
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,580
before a long drive.

73
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:12,900
So no,

74
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,100
it was not magic.

75
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:15,280
It was physiology,

76
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:17,320
pushed to the edge by discipline.

77
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:19,620
And the edge pushed back.

78
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:20,760
On the monitors,

79
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:21,660
his heart slowed,

80
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,820
and it started throwing extra beats.

81
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:26,180
A warning for the record.

82
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:29,240
Breathing hard before going underwater can make you

83
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:31,080
black out with no warning at all.

84
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,720
People drown that way in swimming pools.

85
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,680
Do not try this.

86
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:37,440
Verdict.

87
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:38,520
Months later,

88
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,920
someone broke his record.

89
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,780
Today the record is past twenty-nine minutes.

90
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:44,240
Records fall.

91
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,040
That is not the lesson.

92
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:49,380
The lesson is the distance between seven minutes

93
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,420
and seventeen.

94
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,480
Between the man pulled out of the water,

95
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,440
and the man who came back two years

96
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:55,640
later and stayed under.

97
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,920
He was not born different.

98
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:59,520
He built different.

99
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,460
One breath at a time.

100
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,320
Built Different.

101
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,440
Produced by Relentless Aaron.

